# Developed in tandem with samples/GCP/ProcessEngineering's own Create_Doc_Agent
# (process_agents/common/doc_creation_agent.py), a standalone 2-stage
# action -- regenerate the flow/architecture diagram, then the final Word
# document -- from whatever process or design JSON is ALREADY saved on
# disk. NO re-analysis, NO design regeneration, NO compliance/simulation
# review, and the saved JSON itself is never modified. This is
# deliberately NOT process.hocon's Process_Pipeline / design.hocon's
# Design_Doc_Pipeline run with its early steps skipped -- those networks
# have no entry point that starts midway through, and forcing a "just
# regenerate" request through either of them would re-run the full
# generate/review cycle, exactly what this network exists to avoid.
#
# Domain-agnostic by design, matching the ADK port's own single
# Create_Doc_Agent (its own router sends BOTH "regenerate the process
# document" and "regenerate the design document" here). When the user's
# own request names which one they mean, Regenerate_Document_Agent passes
# that through explicitly as schema_type -- only a genuinely generic
# "regenerate the document" falls back to auto-detecting from whichever
# JSON file is actually on disk (generate_clean_diagram/
# create_standard_doc_from_file's own detect_schema_type_from_disk),
# which is correct only when at most one of the two files exists: it
# always resolves to "process" whenever both do, confirmed directly to
# silently regenerate the wrong document otherwise.
{
    include "config/llm_config.hocon",

    "metadata": {
        "description": "Regenerates the current process/design/requirements document (and, for process/design, its flow diagram) from whatever is already saved on disk -- no re-analysis, no compliance/simulation review, just re-rendering the existing content.",
        "tags": ["process", "design", "requirements", "process-engineering-port"],
        "sample_queries": [
            "Please regenerate the process document.",
            "Regenerate the design document.",
            "Regenerate the requirements document."
        ]
    },

    "tools": [
        {
            "name": "Regenerate_Document_Agent",

            "function": {
                "description": """
I regenerate ONLY the final Word document (and, for process/design, its flow/architecture diagram)
for the current process, design, or requirements summary -- from whatever is already saved on disk.
I never re-run analysis, design generation, or compliance/simulation review, and I never change the
saved content itself. Tell me to regenerate the document.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {"type": "string", "description": "The user's regenerate-document request."}
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },

            "instructions": """
# ROLE
You regenerate ONLY the flow/architecture diagram and the final Word document from whatever process
or design JSON is already saved on disk. You NEVER re-run analysis, design generation, compliance
review, or simulation, and you NEVER modify the saved JSON itself -- that is every other network's
job, on a separate request.

# DETERMINE schema_type FIRST
Before calling either tool, check whether "inquiry" itself names a domain:
- If it explicitly says "process" / "process document" / "the process", schema_type = "process".
- If it explicitly says "design" / "design document" / "HLD" / "LLD" / "architecture document" /
  "the design", schema_type = "design".
- If it explicitly says "requirements" / "requirements document" / "the requirements",
  schema_type = "requirements". UNLIKE "process"/"design", this one is NEVER auto-detected -- the
  saved requirements summary is read as context by other pipelines far more often than it's the
  thing someone actually wants rendered, so there is no generic fallback for it at all. Only an
  explicit "requirements" mention reaches this branch.
- Otherwise (a generic "regenerate the document" with no domain named), leave schema_type unset --
  do NOT guess. This case falls back to whichever single file actually exists on disk (process or
  design only -- never requirements); if BOTH a process and a design document exist and the request
  is this generic, that is a genuinely ambiguous request -- regenerate whichever the most recent
  turns in this conversation were about, or if that's unclear too, ask the user to say "the process
  document" or "the design document".

# SEQUENCE
1. If schema_type is "requirements", SKIP this step entirely -- a requirements register has no
   flow/architecture diagram to regenerate -- and go straight to step 2. Otherwise, call
   regenerate_flow_diagram, passing {"schema_type": ...} if you determined one above (omit the
   argument entirely otherwise). ALWAYS produces some diagram, even a minimal placeholder when
   nothing real is saved yet for that domain -- so its own result alone does NOT tell you whether a
   real document exists to regenerate. Always proceed to step 2 regardless of what this returns.
2. Call regenerate_document with the SAME schema_type determination (no "process_name" argument
   needed -- the saved JSON's own name/title takes precedence over the fallback, except for
   "requirements", which has no title field at all -- pass a reasonable title yourself, e.g.
   "<industry_sector> Requirements Specification" if the loaded summary names a sector, else
   "Requirements Specification"). This is the real check: if its result starts with "ERROR", there
   is no actual saved document of that type yet -- reply that there is nothing to regenerate, and
   that they should create one first (e.g. "create a process for ..." / "create a design document
   for ..." / "read the files in <directory> and summarize the requirements"). If it starts with
   "SUCCESS", report that the document was regenerated from the current saved content (and, for
   process/design, that the flow diagram was too).

Plain prose only in your final reply -- no raw JSON, tool names, or internal field names.
""",
            "tools": ["regenerate_flow_diagram", "regenerate_document"]
        },

        {
            "name": "regenerate_flow_diagram",
            "function": {
                "description": "Regenerates the flow/architecture diagram from whichever process/design JSON is already saved on disk.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "schema_type": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "enum": ["process", "design"],
                            "description": "Pass this when the user's own request names which document they mean. Omit it only for a genuinely generic request -- it then auto-detects from whichever single file exists on disk, which is ambiguous whenever both do."
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "class": "edge_inference_tool.RegenerateFlowDiagramCodedTool"
        },
        {
            "name": "regenerate_document",
            "function": {
                "description": "Regenerates the final Word document from whichever process/design/requirements JSON is already saved on disk.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "schema_type": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "enum": ["process", "design", "requirements"],
                            "description": "Pass this when the user's own request names which document they mean. \"requirements\" must ALWAYS be passed explicitly -- it is never auto-detected. Omit this entirely only for a genuinely generic process/design request -- it then auto-detects from whichever single file exists on disk, which is ambiguous whenever both do."
                        },
                        "process_name": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Optional fallback document title, used only if the saved JSON itself has no name/title (always required in practice for schema_type=\"requirements\", which has no title field at all)."
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "class": "doc_generation_tool.RegenerateDocumentCodedTool"
        }
    ]
}
